# New Feature Checklist

When adding or changing a user-facing library feature, update both demo surfaces before considering the work complete.

## 1. Playground — interactive demo

**File:** `playground/src/pages/PlaygroundPage.tsx`

- Add controls or a demo section so the feature can be toggled and visually verified
- Wire the feature into the live cursor config and code snippet output
- Run `pnpm playground` and confirm the feature works in the browser

## 2. Getting Started — usage docs

**File:** `playground/src/pages/GettingStartedPage.tsx`

- Add a code example (`CodeBlock`) showing how to use the feature
- Update the presets table, feature list, or relevant section if the feature affects documented API surface

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — ships spring physics in src/ but playground/docs unchanged

// ✅ GOOD — feature PR includes:
//   src/core/spring.ts          (implementation)
//   playground/src/pages/PlaygroundPage.tsx   (physics sliders + demo)
//   playground/src/pages/GettingStartedPage.tsx (physics code example)
```

## Scope

Applies to new presets, hooks, components, config options, and behavior changes visible to consumers. Pure internal refactors with no API or UX change are exempt.
